#. Lektion im Kurs „9. Lust und Körperwissen mit Vulva“
#. EN: Discussions of the cervix often come with sweeping promises. Here we begin with the body itself: location, sensitivity and differences in experience. This community question gets a framework in which curiosity and clear boundaries can sit alongside each other.
#. EN:
#. EN: The cervix is the lower, narrow part of the womb and reaches into the top of the vagina. With a finger you can feel it as a firm bump with a small opening, the cervical os.
#. EN:
#. EN: Anatomy, short and clear
#. EN: The os is very narrow and usually filled with mucus. During sex nothing enters the womb; one presses against the cervix or the vaginal vault. The vagina is roughly seven to ten centimetres deep, with big differences. Position, tilt and mobility are individual. A womb tilted backwards is normal.
#. EN:
#. EN: What happens during arousal
#. EN: Well documented: the vagina lengthens and the womb rises a little. That creates more room. The often-quoted claim that the womb becomes much larger could not be confirmed in magnetic resonance studies. Deeper contact need not feel pleasant even during arousal. Your comfort determines whether and how far you wish to go.
#. EN:
#. EN: Sensations
#. EN: The cervix has a good nerve supply (pelvic nerve, hypogastric nerve and the vagus nerve, which bypasses the spinal cord). “Insensitive” is therefore wrong. That does not mean it is pleasurable for everyone. Many experience pressure there as neutral or unpleasant, and that is completely normal.
#. EN:
#. EN: Is there a cervical orgasm?
#. EN: There are credible reports of deep, slowly rising sensations. The research is thin: few small studies, mostly from one research group, for example with women after spinal cord injury, where the vagus nerve seems to play a role. It is not recognised as a separate type of orgasm, and there are no reliable figures on how often it occurs. You do not have to experience it, and it is not “deeper” or “better”. Some coaches and guides claim much more: that the cervix is numb in many people and “wakes up” through daily practice, or that special messenger substances are released. That is not proven.
#. EN:
#. EN: Cycle and life phases
#. EN: Around ovulation the cervix sits higher and is softer, before and during the period lower and firmer. Many feel depth as more painful on some days; this is individual. Dryness and discomfort can increase around menopause. A gynaecologist can help assess treatment options, which may include lubricant or local hormone treatment depending on the situation.
#. EN:
#. EN: When help makes sense
#. EN: Deep pain during sex can point to endometriosis, inflammation, cysts or tension. Bleeding after sex outside your period, discharge with an odour, fever or lower abdominal pain should be checked by a doctor. Do not “push through”.
msgctxt "lesson:female_6#content"
msgid ""
"Über den Gebärmutterhals wird oft mit großen Versprechen gesprochen. Hier beginnen wir mit dem Körper selbst: seiner Lage, seiner Empfindsamkeit und den Unterschieden im Erleben. Die Frage aus der Community bekommt damit einen Rahmen, in dem Neugier und klare Grenzen nebeneinander Platz haben.\n"
