#. EN: Why it works
#. EN: The sphincter is designed to close when pressed from the outside. Pushing triggers counter-tension and pain – and with it, immediately, the brake from course 1. Calm breathing and time can support conscious release; they do not replace willingness or make penetration automatically possible. The principle of this whole program applies especially clearly here: pressure closes, safety opens.
